s and county extension office's then  I return back to Ithaca and but along  the route i make predetermined stops at  orange westchester and nassau county's  on each of our trips so so this is our  one of our stops we stopped at the at  farmingdale College in Nassau County I'm  also i also stopped at Hofstra  University when I'm down there and  planting fields Arboretum as well so  it's not too terrible planting fields  you may recognize that's a very famous  up site that's often taken photos of  planting field and then one of the other  sites we stopped at was we I go to a  cemetery in Westchester County scouting  in the cemetery some cemeteries are very  barren but this particular one has a  nice mix of trees and shrubs and luckily  they don't treat anything so that's good  for me another day of the week I go to  the western part of New York State I go  to Finger Lakes Community College which  has a nice little Arboretum there and  that's in Wayne County and then I also  go to highland park in Monroe County so  and I revisit these specific sites in  this state so that's the same sites all  the time so I have an idea of what i'm  looking for each spot but you know i get  surprises all the time and just keep it  an eye out for things that aren't  looking good if seeing a little  off-color little browning or something  and or you know sometimes I'm looking  and I'm seeing a lot of maybe answer  flies or or something and I'm like oh  there's a lot of honeydew over there  what's happening with that plant so so  by revisiting these specific sites and  doing the on-site scouting I can keep it  good you know  monitoring those pest populations on a  regular basis and can keep a good eye  out for that and then we then I also  have several sites in the area that I  scout on including my own property which  is an abandoned Christmas tree farm so  when my husband I bought that property  eight years ago George asked me if we  had paid extra because of all the great  diseases I 