om  New York State or the New England states  but we have a handful from other states  including Ohio and Michigan and Illinois  addition to the newsletter we also  published a book so it's a 150 updated  feature articles it's about 300 page  book and that is thirty-five dollars  which is to kind of finish up I think  some of the things that we were really  noticing this season that seems some of  the highlights our winter injury we're  seeing a lot of desiccation on spruce  and troopers this spring so we had a  nice article in the last issue in issue  number three Sandra Jensen from the  diagnostic lab wrote a nice article all  about the desiccation on conifers and so  that we're getting a bunch of questions  on and right now what we're seeing out  in the field as this is a time season  for different for us to be sporulating  so there's lots of cedar roster out  there and their full glory and white  pine blister rust is check on it just  finishing up but we've got pine pine  gall rust coming and from Don gable  death on in the Botanic Garden in New  Orca said that he thinks it's going to  be a banner year for cedar rust from  what he was seeing so and then the other  interesting tidbit was we got a report  from Long Island that box of leaf miner  was emerging rather early this year so  it's really a couple  weeks earlier than we expected but it  came from a very reliable source and he  even saw the pupil cases so we're sure  that you know is what he's seeing but so  we're um so I had a conversation with  dan gilleon and we were both surprised  that it was coming out a little early  but we've always include that in this  week's scouting report and that's the  source stuff that we like to put in  things that are you know maybe slightly  unusual and so we do welcome anything  that's you know happening in your county  we'd love to hear any information  especially if you've got outbreak  situation of something we'd like to  share that with our readers so they know  what's going on in the state and it's  nice for us because we can't be  everywhere oh I scout in many places  it's really just a snapshot in time and  i can't i can't go to all the sites in  new york state but so anything that if  you you know if you're what if you'd  like to share with us we'd be willing to  take any information that you have to  share so i'm sure you've all seen the  problems with blue spruce that continues  there are no way there's no one answer  unfortunately for on that one but so  we're kind of keeping an eye on seeing  what's happening with the blue spruce  this season it's been kind of a problem  for the last couple of years i know many  of you have seen that as well and and  we're seeing down in the lower hudson  valley a lot more is it spruce bud go  Mitch then yes I suspect we've been  seeing it for a while and we didn't know  what we were looking at we were finding  all kinds of other things as well and  that was good enough you know what I  mean in a sense you're saying oh it's  got this and it's got that now that  we're looking for it we're finding it in  a lot of spruce samples Norway spruce  okay yeah yeah we were you know we've  put a little bit of information about  that and the newsletter a couple does  the last couple of years Dan Gilmore has  been very helpful with that thank you  this has been a production of Cornell  University on the web at cornell edu

